      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. so for the social democrat side, could you expand more on the \"corrective redistribution\" part? i want to make sure i get the nuance right. does it basically mean that because the initial distribution of wealth is seen as inherently unfair or accidental, the state has a moral obligation to fix it to achieve true justice? i'm trying to see if there's a stronger philosophical way to frame that than just \"helping the poor.\"\nun no,ily tell ican",
